  "term": "abstinence syndrome",
  "definition": "Abstinence syndrome is a group of symptoms that can appear after stopping an abused substance. The signs differ by substance and can include irritability, shaking, and vomiting, and the course depends on how well the withdrawal symptoms are managed.",
